######################################################################
### SORU 33/50 ###
Write a short story (150-200 words) about a locksmith who can open any lock except the one to his own house.
######################################################################

In the heart of bustling downtown, there lived a master locksmith named Eliot. Known for his unparalleled skills, he could pick almost any lock with ease. Yet, there was one door in this world that remained stubbornly closed—his own front door.

Eliot’s home stood on a quiet street, its windows always shuttered at night. Neighbors whispered about the man who never came out after dark, though they marveled at his ability to unlock every other door in town. One stormy evening, as lightning illuminated the sky, Eliot finally decided to face his secret. He approached his own door, tools ready, but no matter how many times he tried, the lock refused to budge. Panic set in as thunder rumbled ominously overhead.

With trembling hands, Eliot called a friend, a retired detective known for solving impossible cases. The detective arrived just as rain began to pour. Together, they examined the door, but even their combined expertise couldn’t find a way inside. That night, Eliot learned that some locks were meant only to be opened from within.

