### SORU 36/50 ###
A coworker just learned their position is being eliminated in a company restructuring. Write what you would say to them.
######################################################################

I'm really sorry to hear about the changes happening at work and that your role might be affected by this restructuring. It's completely understandable if you're feeling worried or uncertain right now.

Firstly, know that it’s normal to have a range of emotions during times like these. Take some time to process how you’re feeling—maybe talk things over with someone close to you for support. If there are any resources available through HR or employee assistance programs, consider reaching out to see how they can help you navigate this transition.

The good news is that while your specific role may no longer exist, companies often provide support for employees going through similar situations. This could include career counseling, job placement services, or even internal opportunities within other departments where skills from your previous role might still be valuable.

In terms of next steps, try to stay focused on your current responsibilities as much as possible. Use this period to learn new skills or take on additional projects that align well with potential future roles. Also, keep an open line of communication with management; they will likely want feedback on how best to assist you during this transition.

Remember, change can also bring unexpected opportunities. Sometimes, stepping into something different leads to personal growth and exciting new challenges. I wish you all the best as you move forward. Let me know if there's anything specific ways I can support you too.

