######################################################################
### SORU 43/50 ###
Write a short story (150-200 words) about a lighthouse keeper's apprentice who is afraid of the dark.
######################################################################

In the quaint coastal village of Marisport, young Eliot served as an apprentice to his father, Keeper Thompson, at the old stone lighthouse perched on the cliff’s edge. Despite his love for the sea and the rhythmic sound of waves crashing against the rocks below, Eliot was terrified of the darkness that crept in after nightfall.

Every evening, as the sun dipped beneath the horizon, Eliot would tremble with fear, clutching tightly to his lantern. His father reassured him, telling stories of how the light guided ships safely through stormy nights. But nothing could quell Eliot’s dread until one fateful night when a fierce storm threatened to engulf the coastline.

With his father injured from falling debris, it fell upon Eliot to keep the beacon burning. As he climbed the winding staircase into the tower, each step echoed louder than the last, amplifying his fears. Reaching the top, he ignited the lamp, its warm glow dispelling the shadows. For the first time, Eliot felt a sense of pride and courage. The next morning, his father praised him, and Eliot realized that facing his fears had made him stronger.

